        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Santo Domingo</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1496 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founded by Bartholomew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> in 1496 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> as La Nueva Isabela, and officially dated from 5 August 1498; the city was rebuilt on the other side of the Ozama after a hurricane in 1502.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the southern coast of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> Sea, at the mouth of the Ozama River, in the present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The first seat of Spanish colonial rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>; the first cathedral, castle, monastery, fortress and university of the New World; the launching point of expeditions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> and the Pacific; the first major slave revolt in the Americas in 1521; Drake's capture in 1586; the years as Ciudad Trujillo</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Santo Domingo is the capital and largest city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>, coterminous with the Distrito Nacional, and its Colonial Zone is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
